<h1>Community Packs</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Curated skill collections -- browse, install, create your own, and contribute.</p>

    <h2 id="what-are-packs">What Are Packs?</h2>

    <p>A pack is a collection of related skills bundled together with a <code>pack.json</code> manifest. Packs are the primary distribution mechanism for sharing curated knowledge. One <code>install_pack</code> call downloads and installs all skills in a pack, signs them, and rebuilds the search index.</p>

    <p>The community repository at <code>penumbraforge/mcp-librarian-skills</code> hosts curated packs that are maintained, tested, and ready to use. You can also create and distribute your own packs.</p>

    <h2 id="available-packs">Available Packs</h2>

    <p>{{ versions.librarian.packs }} curated packs are available in the community repository. Install any pack with a single tool call &mdash; installs are transactional, so a failure part-way through rolls back instead of leaving your library in a half-written state.</p>

    <p>Contributions to the pack repository are screened in CI before they can merge: a validation script checks pack structure, <code>index.json</code> consistency, and frontmatter, and a content guard scans every submitted skill for prompt-injection patterns. Packs are also signed on install, so a tampered pack file is caught on load.</p>

